  "body": "## What changed\n\ntruck's surface subdivision (`sub_parameter_division`) recurses forever on a B-spline or NURBS face that is not continuous: one seam stays \"far\" at every depth. The recursion runs inside a rayon task that nothing can interrupt, and it produces no facet, so the facet budget never fires. That is the #1536 hang.\n\n- New `crates/app/src/geometry/import/step_guard.rs`. Each face's surface is wrapped in `Metered`, which counts the points truck evaluates on the face in one tessellation pass.\n  - B-spline and NURBS faces are divided by truck's own generic `algo::surface::parameter_division`, called on the wrapper. Their own impls run exactly this algorithm, so the division and the mesh are identical. Other surface kinds keep their specialised division.\n  - Past `FACE_EVAL_CAP` (25 M) evaluations, the wrapper returns one fixed point, so the subdivision stops within one sweep. It also returns the bare range as the division, so truck does not triangulate the runaway grid.\n- `step.rs`: `shell_facets` builds the guarded shell, resets the meters on each pass, and reads them before a held panic is re-raised. A tripped face refuses the import by name, for example: `corrupt STEP: face #53 (B-spline surface, face 6 of 6 in shell #17) could not be tessellated: its surface subdivision did not converge within 25000000 evaluations (a discontinuous or degenerate surface) - re-export the model, or import an STL`.\n- No thread is spawned, and nothing outlives the call. A worker thread with a deadline was rejected: a stranded thread keeps a core busy and its memory grows. Truck itself is not patched. The reasons are in `docs/decisions/1536-step-tess-guard.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nNew fixtures, built by hand from `box.step`:\n- `testdata/models/bspline_discontinuous.step`: the top face is a degree-1 B-spline whose interior knot is repeated, so it jumps 0.25 at u = 0.5. Unguarded, `parameter_division` on it was confirmed still running after 30 s, in both debug and release.\n- `testdata/models/bspline_dome.step`: the top face is a smooth biquadratic dome.\n\nPins, each mutation-checked (each mutation applied, the test seen failing, then reverted):\n\n| Test | Pins | Mutation that fails it |\n|---|---|---|\n| `import_step_guard::a_face_that_never_converges_is_refused_by_name_within_the_budget` | default cap; refused by name in 4.5 s (debug) under a 120 s hard limit | no fixed-point short-circuit (times out); no entity names (`face_entities` mismatch) |\n| `import_step_guard::a_lowered_cap_refuses_the_same_face_at_once` | the refusal names the face and the cap | same two |\n| `import_step_guard::a_smooth_bspline_face_still_imports_closed_at_its_volume` | a B-spline face still imports: volume 1 + 0.2/9, crown at 1.05 | - (regression pin) |\n| `import_step_guard::degenerate_bspline_variants_end_cleanly_and_bounded` | 7 bent knot/multiplicity variants each import or refuse, bounded | no short-circuit (times out) |\n| `step_guard::tests::a_smooth_bspline_divides_exactly_as_truck_does_and_does_not_trip` | the division is identical to truck's own at 3 tolerances | tolerance scaled in the wrapper's division |\n| `step_guard::tests::a_discontinuous_bspline_division_stops_at_the_cap_and_trips_the_meter` | bounded division, empty grid on a trip | the empty-division return removed |\n| `step_guard::tests::nothing_keeps_running_after_a_refused_pass` | no work left running after the call | the tessellation moved to a detached thread (option (c) shape) |\n| `step_guard::tests::the_refusal_names_the_face_its_kind_and_the_cap` | the refusal text | - |\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green in 24 s (app lib plus bore_facet_sagitta, import_step_guard, large_models, model_fidelity, step_budget, step_chord_units, step_fidelity, step_nesting, stock_export). `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test import`: 26 passed. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets --no-deps -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nCap measured in release: a 400 mm doubly curved bicubic patch at the 0.0025 mm chord cap needs 1.5 M evaluations (a 475 x 475 grid). The discontinuous face reaches 25 M in about 1.7 s.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- **The user's `sc_logo.step` was not available to this worker.** This fix is pinned on a synthetic face with the same failure mode (`sub_parameter_division` on a B-spline that never converges), not on the user's file. Re-run the issue's repro (`cam.import(\"sc_logo.step\", ...)`) on a build of this branch. The expected result is a named refusal of one of the 20 corner blends within seconds. If the blends are in fact continuous and only slow, the refusal still comes, but that file would then call for a different fix (better: make them tessellate), and the issue's \"Better, the NURBS blends tessellate\" stays open.\n- Edge-curve and swept-surface divisions are not metered. They are filed as #1545 (P7).\n- The GUI import path was not run by hand. It calls the same `load_model`/`parse_with_chord_budget`.\n\nChangelog: STEP import no longer hangs on a B-spline or NURBS face whose tessellation never converges; the import is refused naming the face, its kind and its shell (#1536)\n\nEffort: high (not escalated)\n\nFork synced at v0.18.0; branched from upstream/main 41cd9c2.\n\nFixes #1536\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
